| `tests/integration/test_committed_secrets_gate.py` | Fails a file a commit could carry that holds a value under a secret name, naming the file, the line and the key and never the value: every name comes from a `scripts/config_loader.py` `KEYS` row with `secret=True`, a file matching `secrets.json_files` is judged as JSON at any depth and one matching `secrets.dotenv_files` as `KEY=VALUE` lines, and its work-tree copy and its index copy are both judged. The empty value is the only placeholder. It also fails a `models.credential_env` variable with no secret row, a secret row with a default, a secret variable in `child_env.names`, a judged JSON file that does not parse, and a run that judged no name or no file, so a new credential cannot pass by having no row. | `make test` | [`secrets.dotenv_files`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`secrets.json_files`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Sees a name, not a shape: a credential under a name no secret row declares, in a file type it does not parse, in an ignored file, or already in history is not its to see. Not a scanner for key-shaped strings. | [CONVENTIONS.md](../../CONVENTIONS.md) | always |
